; Configurations met under an old period are forgotten when it grows.  The run
; walks (at 1) to (at 4) one successor at a time, period 1.  At (at 4), turn 3,
; it meets two successors, the period becomes 2, and it takes successor 1, back
; to (at 2) at turn 4.  It was at (at 2) at turn 1, an odd turn: not the same
; configuration, though under period 1 both had phase 0.  At turn 6 (at 4)
; takes successor 0, (at 0), and the run ends.
(step one)
(observe run)
(schedule rotating)
(at 1)
(rule a (take (at 1)) (make (at 2)))
(rule b (take (at 2)) (make (at 3)))
(rule c (take (at 3)) (make (at 4)))
(rule back (take (at 4)) (make (at 2)))
(rule out (take (at 4)) (make (at 0)))
